{"ts":"2026-08-08T08:00:22.880Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"79fe526b1f45937aac208eb8","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"1","source":"environment"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.226","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-3lhth4"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Host environment faults escape untyped at every filesystem boundary except the one just guarded, and the recurrence is only ever discovered as a production error that blocks a release"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Snapshot create and restore now translate host filesystem faults into declared refusals, but that boundary is one of roughly thirty-two await-ed filesystem calls across core and sdk, and it is the only one that has it. Everywhere else an ENOSPC, EACCES, EROFS, EDQUOT or platform-specific errno propagates as a raw Node error: it reaches the user as a stack-shaped message naming a scrubbed syscall frame, it carries no declared code, and it is reported as an unexpected production exception. The observability record shows this is a family and not an incident. Four of the fifteen most recent production issues are exactly this shape — ENOSPC copyfile, EACCES open, EISDIR read, and an unknown system error -122 — each filed, triaged and resolved as an individual defect, with nothing in the graph or in CI relating them. The cost is asymmetric: because these events are indistinguishable from genuine defects, each one enters the release reliability window as unclassifiable and blocks every scheduled cut until a human resolves it by hand, which is what happened on 2026-08-08. The missing artifacts are a shared translation primitive at the IO boundary and a gate that fails when a new unguarded filesystem call site is introduced, so the family stops being rediscovered one production error at a time. Duplicate check searched raw errno boundary, environment fault typed refusal and filesystem error taxonomy across all statuses; pm-j668gl owns errno string literals in the Windows test suite and pm-4odf0c owned the single snapshot instance, neither owns the boundary or the gate."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:observability","area:sdk","area:storage","error-taxonomy","gate","recurrence"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-08T08:00:22.880Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-08T08:00:22.880Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":300},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"One shared primitive translates host filesystem and resource errno faults into declared PmCliError refusals with a bounded operation label, recovery guidance, and no path disclosure; Every awaited filesystem call site in core and sdk either routes through that primitive or carries a recorded waiver naming why the raw fault is correct; A CI gate fails when a new unguarded filesystem call site is added, so the family cannot silently regrow; The declared codes resolve in the generated error catalog, and a negative control proves a non-errno fault still propagates as a defect rather than being swallowed as environment noise"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-o2kc"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-1qkivy","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-08T08:00:22.880Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-4odf0c","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-08T08:00:22.880Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-f05lsg","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-08T08:00:22.880Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-ouyq3n","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-08T08:00:22.880Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-qxo5iu","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-08T08:00:22.880Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-rtn5h6","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-08T08:00:22.880Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-xp1xsw","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-08T08:00:22.880Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"bbbd8510046f4ae97b96a0a9139d0a82e125119cd688c48d05c49b828d0521ff","message":""}
